msgid "Default Component"
msgstr "Töp Komponent"

#. i18n: file componentchooser_ui.ui line 46
#: rc.cpp:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can change the component program. Components are programs that handle "
"basic tasks, like the terminal emulator, the text editor and the email client. "
"Different KDE applications sometimes need to invoke a console emulator, send a "
"mail or display some text. To do so consistently, these applications always "
"call the same components. You can choose here which programs these components "
"are."
msgstr ""
"Bonda komponent-yazılımnarnı saylap bula. Komponent digäne ul berär töp eşne "
"eşli torğan yazılımdır, ü.ö. terminal, yazma tözätkeç, email kliente. KDE'neñ "
"törle yazılımnarğa qayçaqta terminal täräzäse, xat cibärergä, berär yazma "
"tözätergä kiräk bula, ul çaqta şul komponentlar çaqırıla da."

#. i18n: file componentchooser_ui.ui line 75
#: rc.cpp:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Component Description"
msgstr "Komponent Açıqlaması"

#. i18n: file componentchooser_ui.ui line 78
#: rc.cpp:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can read a small description of the currently selected component. To "
"change the selected component, click on the list to the left. To change the "
"component program,  please choose it below."
msgstr ""
"Biredä saylanğan komponent turında qısqa açıqlamasın bonda uqıp bula. Berär "
"componentne saylaw öçen, sul tezmägä çirtäse. Ul komponent yazılımın üzgärtü "
"öçen, anı asqaraq saylísı."

#. i18n: file componentchooser_ui.ui line 119
#: rc.cpp:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<qt>\n"
"<p>This list shows the configurable component types. Click the component you "
"want to configure.</p>\n"
"<p>In this dialog you can change KDE default components. Components are "
"programs that handle basic tasks, like the terminal emulator, the text editor "
"and the email client. Different KDE applications sometimes need to invoke a "
"console emulator, send a mail or display some text. To do so consistently, "
"these applications always call the same components. Here you can select which "
"programs these components are.</p>\n"
"</qt>"
msgstr ""
"<qt>\n"
"<p>Komponentneñ caylap bulğan törlären bu tezmädä kürep bula. Berärsen caylaw "
"öçen anın östenä çirtäse.</p>\n"
"<p>KDE'neñ töp komponentlären bu täräzädä caylap bula. Komponent digäne ul "
"berär töp eş eşli torğan yazılımdır, ü.ö. terminal, yazma tözätkeç, email "
"kliente. KDE'neñ berär yazılımına terminal täräzäse, xat cibärergä, berär yazma "
"tözätergä kiräk bulğan çaqta şul komponentlär çaqırıla.</p>\n"
"</qt>"

#. i18n: file emailclientconfig_ui.ui line 83
#: rc.cpp:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ul> "
"<li>%t: Recipient's address</li> "
"<li>%s: Subject</li> "
"<li>%c: Carbon Copy (CC)</li> "
"<li>%b: Blind Carbon Copy (BCC)</li> "
"<li>%B: Template body text</li> "
"<li>%A: Attachment </li> </ul>"
msgstr ""
"<ul> "
"<li>%t: Aluçı adrese</li> "
"<li>%s: Tarmaq</li> "
"<li>%c: Karbon Küpläw (CC)</li> "
"<li>%b: Suqır Karbon Küpläw (BCC)</li> "
"<li>%B: Waqıtlı tän eçtälege</li> "
"<li>%A: Qıstırma </li> </ul>"

#. i18n: file emailclientconfig_ui.ui line 86
#: rc.cpp:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to select your favorite email client. Please note that the "
"file you select has to have the executable attribute set in order to be "
"accepted."
"<br> You can also use several placeholders which will be replaced with the "
"actual values when the email client is called:"
"<ul> "
"<li>%t: Recipient's address</li> "
"<li>%s: Subject</li> "
"<li>%c: Carbon Copy (CC)</li> "
"<li>%b: Blind Carbon Copy (BCC)</li> "
"<li>%B: Template body text</li> "
"<li>%A: Attachment </li> </ul>"
msgstr ""
"Yaratılğan email klienten saylaw öçen bu töymägä çirtäse. Saylanğan bulası "
"birem eşçän itep bilgelängän bulğanın tikşerep alası."
"<br> Berniçä köylämä almaştırğıçların qullanıp bula, cibärelgän çaqta alar "
"urınına çın bäyä salınaçaq:"
"<ul> "
"<li>%t: Aluçınıñ adrese</li> "
"<li>%s: Tarmaq</li> "
"<li>%c: Küçermä (CC)</li> "
"<li>%b: Suqır Küçermä (BCC)</li> "
"<li>%B: Çorlı tän eçtälege</li> "
"<li>%A: Qıstırma </li> </ul>"

